        "id": 1001350
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-07T13:59:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After some discussions internally, the developer is left to do their own integration script.\n\nFWIW, I think we should be providing an integration script, so perhaps it\u0027s better for @balint.dobszay@arm.com @sandrine.afsa@arm.com to give their opinion on why we shouldn\u0027t.",
      "parentUuid": "5b13c388_0c6c94f6",
      "revId": "6c7d06cb33265f82a97719c5aaf74f8681bc3a21",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ac5ba3e_47ee3d94",
        "filename": "README.md",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000309
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-07T14:10:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Everyone writing their own scripts doesn\u0027t seem like a good developer experience. If we\u0027re removing the integration from the RF-A Makefile (which is reasonable) then I really think we should be providing it somewhere else in a consistent way, like we agreed before.\n\nGetting started with RF-A should ideally be as simple as checking out a single repository (with submodules or similar for TF-A and RF-A itself) and running a single command (either a script or a make command or something equivalent), which should build everything necessary for the chosen platform and run the tests (at least for QEMU and FVP).",
      "parentUuid": "7f9b9665_ed663f21",
      "revId": "6c7d06cb33265f82a97719c5aaf74f8681bc3a21",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8cbab93_1026861d",
        "filename": "README.md",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000160
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-08T09:23:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s okay to move this into a separate script for now. Regarding the integration repo, recently in internal discussions we have started questioning whether we\u0027re willing to accept the additional maintenance effort for that. Even if it starts as a simple script, it is likely to evolve and increase in scope during the years, and probably end up as yet another tool next to the already existing ones. Partners will use Yocto, Buildroot, etc or their own integration system anyway, and RF-A is just another component there. We already provide the CI scripts which can be used as a reference on how to build everything. Also, we plan to add RF-A support to [Shrinkwrap](https://gitlab.arm.com/tooling/shrinkwrap), which is a simple integration system that can build various A-profile reference configurations (3 world, 4 world, etc). It already has support for the existing TF-A tests, we can add STF as well.",
      "parentUuid": "4ac5ba3e_47ee3d94",
      "revId": "6c7d06cb33265f82a97719c5aaf74f8681bc3a21",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
